From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0431-gfx-02-buffer-collector-mark.patch

Source: 0431-gfx-02-buffer-collector-mark.patch
buffer collector from a lower mark

Core patch on core-t33 (T35 stack), off unless EDEN_NX2_BC_COLLECT_MIB is set.

For Switch 2 titles the buffer cache collects only when its buffers hold 512 MiB or more (in
earnest at 1 GiB). Zelda's buffers on the console held 282 to 324 MiB while walking and 457 MiB
8 s after an area change (run 149), so the collector never ran and nothing unused was ever given
back. EDEN_NX2_BC_COLLECT_MIB=256 runs it from 256 MiB: the gentle collector, which deletes
buffers no draw used for 120 frames, 32 a frame, and leaves every buffer holding GPU-written data
alone, so there is no download and no wait for the GPU. From twice the mark the aggressive one
runs as before (60 frames, 64 a frame, GPU-written buffers downloaded first).

Logs once "EDEN_NX2_BC_COLLECT_MIB=256: the buffer collector runs from 256 MiB, in earnest from
512 MiB". Proof is the "Buffer cache: N buffers M MiB" line every 600 frames and
EDEN_REFUSED_BUFFERS in a refusal report, against run 149's 457 MiB.

Trade: a buffer deleted and needed again is made and uploaded again. Unset, 512 MiB as before.
Not built, not run.

 src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h | 17 +++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
index c3d17b983b..99406bdd99 100644
--- a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
@@ -173,8 +173,21 @@ void BufferCache<P>::TickFrame() {
         // downloading the GPU-written ones, ~5% of the GPU thread) that were recreated later.
         // Collect when the buffers themselves are large. At 1 GiB it held geometry of scenes
         // long gone: title 1's title screen grew to ~0.9 GB of buffers in ten minutes.
-        if (buffer_bytes >= 512_MiB) {
-            RunGarbageCollector(buffer_bytes >= 1_GiB);
+        // EDEN_NX2_BC_COLLECT_MIB=<MiB> (unset: 512, as before) lowers the mark: on the console
+        // Ocarina of Time's buffers held 280 to 460 MiB, so this never ran there. Below twice the
+        // mark it is the gentle collector: buffers unused for 120 frames, 32 a frame, none
+        // holding GPU-written data, so no download and no wait for the GPU.
+        static const u64 collect_mark = [] {
+            const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_BC_COLLECT_MIB");
+            const u64 mib = value != nullptr ? std::strtoull(value, nullptr, 10) : 0;
+            if (mib != 0) {
+                LOG_INFO(HW_GPU, "EDEN_NX2_BC_COLLECT_MIB={}: the buffer collector runs from {} MiB, in earnest from {} MiB",
+                         value, mib, 2 * mib);
+            }
+            return (mib != 0 ? mib : u64{512}) << 20;
+        }();
+        if (buffer_bytes >= collect_mark) {
+            RunGarbageCollector(buffer_bytes >= 2 * collect_mark);
         }
     } else if (total_used_memory >= minimum_memory) {
         RunGarbageCollector(total_used_memory >= critical_memory);
